Serve ATAPI from the disc model when the medium is a cdimage (doc 17
§5.3–5.4, M5 steps 5 and 6): hw/ide/atapi.c asks cdimage_disc(blk_bs(s->blk))
on every command; NULL keeps today's code path byte for byte (a plain ISO
on the raw driver). With a model: READ(10)/(12) are L-EC-verified cooked
reads that refuse audio (05/64/00) and fail bad sectors (03/11/05); READ
CD / READ CD MSF accept the full MMC-3 field table incl. C2 pointers and
the three subchannel forms; READ TOC formats 0/1/2, READ SUB-CHANNEL
1/2/3, READ DISC INFORMATION come from libdisc's responders; GET
CONFIGURATION reports a CD-ROM drive with CD read (C2) and CD audio
features, mode page 2A a 48x CD-DA-capable drive, page 0E the audio
ports; MODE SELECT(10) (a data-out packet command, PIO or DMA) sets page
0E; PLAY AUDIO (10/12/MSF/TRACK-INDEX), PAUSE/RESUME and STOP play the
audio sectors through the ide-cd device's new `audiodev=` (a 44100 Hz
stereo voice fed sector by sector with page 0E's routing and volume) or,
without one, track a position at 75 sectors per second of virtual time;
INQUIRY names the ide-cd `model` property. The PIO loop fills each
sector synchronously from the model; the DMA path fills whole chunks and
re-enters through a bottom half. REQUEST SENSE carries an ASCQ. The new
IDEState fields are not migrated (snapshots with a cdimage medium are
unsupported). CDIMAGE_TRACE=1 prints every packet, reply and sense.

